- name: seg_b_scope
  id: qtgui_time_sink_x
  parameters:
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    autoscale: 'False'
    axislabels: 'True'
    comment: 'SEGMENT B is the on-chip NEGATIVE CONTROL and it is SUPPOSED to fail. Same chip, same run, same chain - only
      the SNR is 20 dB worse. Red X marks (decoded) scattering away from their dark-red circles (transmitted) is the INTENDED
      result: it is what proves segment A''s SER 0 above is a real measurement and not a chain that cannot fail. A clean overlay
      HERE would mean the control is broken. B draws only in the RIGHT half of the sweep.'
    ctrlpanel: 'False'
    entags: 'True'
    grid: 'False'
    gui_hint: 2,0,1,2
    legend: 'True'
    name: '''SEGMENT B  ·  −10 dB  ·  NEGATIVE CONTROL  —  the X marks MISS their circles, SER ≈ 0.63  ✓ EXPECTED, THIS IS
      THE POINT'''
